          <Pad Id="GbyNiuQCqepPIXKGsl3U0H" Bounds="-581,2734,488,495" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Role: Concept and vocabulary chapter. Opens Part V.&#xD;&#xA;Core idea: A data type can bundle properties together, similar to how Vector (Join) and Vector (Split) bundle X, Y, Z — but with custom names, custom operations, and your choice of what goes inside.&#xD;&#xA;What lands:&#xD;&#xA;An object = data + operations bundled together&#xD;&#xA;The reader has been using objects since chapter 10 (Circle, Rectangle, Material) and defining objects since chapter 11 (Process nodes)&#xD;&#xA;Record introduced as the default way to define a custom data type in VL&#xD;&#xA;How to define a Record via the Node Browser or Patch Explorer&#xD;&#xA;Light scratch at operations and mutability — enough to give the reader the vocabulary they'll meet again&#xD;&#xA;Closes with a forward pointer to Class as another flavor coming in chapter 42&#xD;&#xA;Carrying example: A tiny Record with two or three properties — small enough to feel obvious, big enough to be inspectable. Not yet the Particle.&#xD;&#xA;Back-references: ch. 10 (Complex Types), ch. 11 (Process Nodes)&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;IMPORTANT RESOURCES&#xD;&#xA;https://claude.ai/share/c4b342f3-1549-48ad-8b1d-9e6f08ef25b5&#xD;&#xA;https://forum.vvvv.org/t/when-to-pick-a-process-a-record-or-a-class/21624&#xD;&#xA;https://thegraybook.vvvv.org/reference/language/nodes.html&#xD;&#xA;https://thegraybook.vvvv.org/reference/language/operations.html">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
